Description
Learn how to use Jinja2 conditional statements to dynamically modify configuration files based on variables, without changing the template itself. In real-world systems, not all configurations apply everywhere. In this lab Gzip compression should only be enabled in production environments and the same NGINX template must work for both dev and prod. You will achieve this by controlling behavior using variables, not separate templates.

Required Credentials for the Lab:

SSH Credentials: (for remote connection to server1)
SSH Username: server1_admin
SSH Password: server1_admin@123!
Sudo Credentials (for privilege escalation)
Sudo Password: server1_admin@123!
Tasks
1. Create a workspace

Set up /home/user/workspace as your Ansible working directory.
2. Create inventory.ini

Define a web host group containing server1.

Include SSH and sudo credentials for Ansible connectivity.

3. Create a Jinja2 template

File name: /home/user/workspace/nginx.conf.j2

The template must:

Always define a basic NGINX server block

Conditionally include gzip on; only if enable_gzip is true

4. Create an Ansible playbook

File name: conditional-gzip.yml

The playbook must:

Target the web group

Use become: true

Define a variable enable_gzip

Deploy the template to /etc/nginx/nginx.conf

5. Run the playbook twice

First run: enable_gzip: false

Second run: enable_gzip: true

6. Verify behavior

Confirm:

gzip on; is absent when disabled

gzip on; is present when enabled

The template file itself must not change

Expected Outcome
Install Nginx if not already present

One template works for all environments

Gzip is enabled only when required

Configuration is controlled entirely by variables


____________________________________________________________________


tep 1: Create Workspace
mkdir -p /home/user/workspace
cd /home/user/workspace
Step 2: Create inventory.ini
[web]
server1 ansible_host=server1 ansible_user=server1_admin ansible_password=server1_admin@123! ansible_become_password=server1_admin@123!
Step 3: Create Jinja2 Template (nginx.conf.j2)
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name localhost;

    {% if enable_gzip %}
    gzip on;
    gzip_types text/plain text/css application/json;
    {% endif %}

    location / {
        root /var/www/html;
        index index.html;
    }
}
Step 4: Create Playbook (conditional-gzip.yml)
- hosts: web
  become: true
  gather_facts: false

  vars:
    enable_gzip: false   # change to true for production

  tasks:
    - name: Install nginx
      package:
        name: nginx
        state: present

    - name: Deploy nginx configuration with conditional gzip
      template:
        src: nginx.conf.j2
        dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
Step 5: Execute Playbook
ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini conditional-gzip.yml

Step 6: Test Production Mode
Edit the playbook:

enable_gzip: true

Re-run:

ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini conditional-gzip.yml